# No Compatibility Shims

When renaming, replacing an API, or adopting new domain language: **use the new names at every call site and delete the old names in the same change.** Do not leave a bridge between old and new.

Persisted data is the exception: migrate stored records with an upgrade command. Do not paper over old columns, fields, or types in application code.

## Do

- Rename identifiers, types, GraphQL fields, files, and comments to the new language
- Update every in-repo caller in the same change
- Delete the old export, type, field, constant, and fallback once callers are updated

## Do not

- Alias old names onto new ones (`export const oldName = newName`)
- Re-export under the previous name (`export { ChatMessage as WhatsAppMessage }`)
- Wrap the new API in a function or type that still uses the old name
- Dual-read / dual-write (`record.chatMessage ?? record.whatsappMessage`)
- Keep `@deprecated` stubs, `*Legacy*` helpers, or `compat` / `shim` modules
- Accept both old and new field names on the same input type

```typescript
// ❌ Shim: old language still exists
export const findWhatsAppMessages = findChatMessages;
type WhatsAppMessage = ChatMessage;
const body = record.chatMessage ?? record.whatsappMessage;

// ✅ New language used directly; old names gone
const body = record.chatMessage;
```
